{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-conjunctive-particle-adversative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational"],"statement":{"en":"The particle siri can function as a conjunctive particle meaning 'even though' or 'despite'.","ja":"助詞 siri は「〜であるのに」「〜にもかかわらず」を意味する接続助詞として機能することがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["siri"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-09","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--shir-grammaticalization-from-noun","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--diachrony"],"statement":{"en":"The form shir, originally a noun meaning 'land' or 'place', has grammaticalized into a prefix-like element expressing surrounding space, weather, and evidentiality.","ja":"shir はもともと「土地・場所」を意味する名詞であったが、周囲の空間や天候、見説法などを表す接頭辞的要素へと文法化した。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["shir","shir-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-action-in-progress-chitose","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--diachrony"],"statement":{"en":"In the Chitose dialect, siri is used to indicate the state or appearance of an action in progress at the reference time.","ja":"千歳方言において、siri は基準時に進行中の動作の状態や様子を表すために用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["at reference time"]},"forms":["siri"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:takahashi2022@handbook-epub/l0121-03","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sir-sentence-final-visual-evidential","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--frames"],"statement":{"en":"When sir(i) is used in a sentence-final phrase, its lexical nominal meaning is bleached and it expresses visually confirmed situations.","ja":"sir(i) は文末句で用いられると名詞的意味が消失し、視覚的に確認された事態を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["in sentence-final position"]},"forms":["siri","sir"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0393-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-explaining-own-action","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--frames"],"statement":{"en":"siri ne can be used to explain the speaker's own current action or situation as reflected in the addressee's eyes.","ja":"siri ne は、相手の目に映っている現在の話し手自身の行為や状況を説明するために用いられることがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":["explaining current situation to addressee"]},"forms":["siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0393-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-interrogatives-addressee-action","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--frames"],"statement":{"en":"In interrogative clauses, siri and siri an are used to ask about an action in which the addressee is currently engaged.","ja":"疑問文において、siri および siri an は相手が現在行っている行為について尋ねる際に用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["in interrogative clauses"]},"forms":["siri","siri an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0394-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sittapan-parallel-to-siri-ne","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--frames"],"statement":{"en":"The usage of sittapan corresponds functionally to the usage of siri ne that explains the speaker's current action to the addressee.","ja":"sittapan の用法は、話し手が現在していることを目の前の相手に説明するという siri ne の用法の一つに対応している。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"epistemic","conditions":[]},"forms":["sittapan","siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0398-03","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-explaining-own-action","differs_in":null,"note":"Parallels siri ne in explaining current action to addressee"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-visual-evidential-southwest","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--paradigm"],"statement":{"en":"In Southwestern Hokkaido Ainu, the complex predicate siri ne functions as a visual evidential meaning 'it looks that'.","ja":"北海道南西方言において、複合述語 siri ne は「〜のようである、〜に見える」という視覚証拠性を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0019-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-visual-perception-hokkaido","differs_in":"scope","note":"Southwestern dialect scope versus general Hokkaido"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--shir-evidential-construction-types","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--paradigm"],"statement":{"en":"In evidential constructions, shir-ki dynamically marks the immediately preceding action or state, shir-iki dynamically marks the broader situation or atmosphere, and shir-an marks a static state.","ja":"見説法構文において、shir-ki は直前の動作・状態を動的に受け、shir-iki は全体の雰囲気・環境を動的に受け、shir-an は静的な状態の存在を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["in evidential constructions"]},"forms":["shir-ki","shir-iki","shir-an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0200-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--nepenepo-siran-visual-versus-humas","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--paradigm"],"statement":{"en":"In népenepo constructions, síran is selected for visual perception whereas húmas is selected for internal sensation.","ja":"népenepo 構文において、視覚に基づく場合には síran が、内部感覚に基づく場合には húmas が選択される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["in népenepo constructions"]},"forms":["húmas","síran"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0343-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sir-witnessed-mood-marker","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--paradigm"],"statement":{"en":"The particle sir is used to express witnessed mood, affirming a fact directly observed by the speaker.","ja":"助詞 sir は、話者が目撃した事実を確認する目撃法を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["sir","siri","sir-an","siri-ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0050-11","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sir-individual-level-restriction-tokachi","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--predication-type"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, sir is not used with individual-level predication describing permanent properties even when visual information is available, and ru is chosen instead.","ja":"十勝方言において、恒常的な性質について述べる個体レベル叙述では視覚情報であっても sir は用いられず、ru が選択される。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["in individual-level predication"]},"forms":["sir","ru"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0004-01","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sir-stage-level-predication-tokachi","differs_in":null,"note":"Negative individual-level restriction complementary to stage-level predication"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sir-restricted-temporary-states-tokachi","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--predication-type"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, sir is restricted to uncompleted events or temporary states.","ja":"十勝方言において、sir は未完結の事象や一時的状態に限定されて用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["sir"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0004-03","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sir-stage-level-predication-tokachi","differs_in":"framework","note":"Descriptive terminology versus formal stage-level semantics"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--sir-stage-level-predication-tokachi","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--predication-type"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, the visual evidential nominalizer sir is used with stage-level predication.","ja":"十勝方言において、視覚的知覚を表す証拠性名詞化辞 sir はステージレベル述語とともに用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["with stage-level predication"]},"forms":["sir"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:takahashi2022@handbook-epub/l0121-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-explicative-recent-completion","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The combination siri ne conveys an explicative nuance meaning 'having just done...'.","ja":"siri ne は断りの意味を表し、「今〜したところだ」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-asserts-present-facts","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The form siri ne (shiri-ne) is used to firmly assert facts present before one's eyes, conveying that something is so or has just occurred.","ja":"siri ne（shiri-ne）は眼前の事実について「〜である」「〜したところである」と確説するのに用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["facts present before one's eyes"]},"forms":["siri ne","shiri-ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-10","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0201-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--kensai-ho-asserts-present-facts","differs_in":null,"note":"shiri-ne specifically as realization of kensai-hō"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-visible-situations","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The form siri ne is used for visible situations.","ja":"siri ne は目に見える状況に関して用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":["visible situations"]},"forms":["siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-04","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-visually-judged-chitose","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"In the Chitose dialect, siri ne is defined as a sentence-final particle indicating that the situation has been judged visually.","ja":"千歳方言において、siri ne は視覚的に判断された状況であることを示す文末詞である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0003-06","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-visual-perception-hokkaido","differs_in":"scope","note":"Chitose dialect specific description versus general Hokkaido"}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-visual-perception-hokkaido","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido Ainu, siri ne typically marks information obtained through visual perception.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語において、siri ne は典型的には視覚から得た情報であることを標示する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"most","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0004-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-ne-unactualized-future-events","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"In Hokkaido Ainu, siri ne can be used when speaking about unactualized future events.","ja":"北海道アイヌ語において、siri ne は実現していない未来の出来事について発言する際にも用いられることがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"assertive","conditions":["unactualized future events"]},"forms":["siri ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:hirosawa2026@pdftotext-pieces/l0004-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--kensai-ho-asserts-present-facts","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The visual evidential category (kensai-hō) serves to firmly assert facts present before one's eyes.","ja":"見説法は眼前の事実に就いて確説するものである。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["shiri-ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0193-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:evidential/siri-ne-situational--siri-hawe-sensory-mode-contrast","revision":1,"topic":"topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topics":["topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational","topic:evidential/siri-ne-situational--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"In the Shizunai dialect, the choice between siri and hawe is determined solely by the sensory modality of perception (visual vs. auditory or other sensory) rather than speaker evaluation.","ja":"静内方言において、siri と hawe の選択は話し手の評価ではなく、言及されている事柄についての知覚様態（視覚的か聴覚的等か）のみによって決定される。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["siri","hawe"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0030-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
